  "provenance": {
    "physical_parameters": {
      "origin": "inferred",
      "note": "Golf 1.6 TDI / EA288-inspired warm common-rail I4. Pole Position Production identifies its 2019 Golf Variant recording as a 1.6 litre four-cylinder turbo diesel: https://pole.se/product/golf-variant-tdi-2019/ . VW Self-study Programme 891143C, The Golf 2014, printed p.20 supplies earlier CLHA-family bore 79.5 mm, stroke 80.5 mm, compression 16.2:1, and four valves: https://www.vaglinks.com/Docs/SSP/VWUSA.COM_SSP_891143C_2014_Golf.pdf . These family dimensions do not identify the exact recorded engine code or ECU calibration. Two 2 mg pilots at -18/-9 degrees and 38 mg main at -1 degree ATDC are authored, all scaled by fueling. Injector needle/rail pressure and ECU schedules are not solved. Rod length, cam windows/areas, gas temperatures, heat transfer, ignition coefficients and steady intake/exhaust boundary map are authored. Load-dependent boost up to 211325 Pa absolute at 2200-2700 RPM represents prescribed reservoirs, not compressor/turbine dynamics or turbo lag; oxygen fraction is fixed and EGR is not solved. No measured power/torque/emissions claim."
    },
    "presentation": {
      "origin": "artistic",
      "note": "Golf character revision after the initial modern audition retained general vibration but lacked detail. Public reference: https://soundcloud.com/polepositionproduction/vw-golf-diesel-t6-onbrd-steady . No reference audio or measured impulse response is embedded. Preserve pilot/main injection, charge-boundary map, firing phases, fuel trims and exhaust dry gain. Authored per-cylinder structural couplings are about .846/.662/.586/.754 in firing order. The previous 1/.56/.38/.78 contrast created excessive whole-engine amplitude modulation heard as flapping. Shrink departures from the mean to 40% and normalize to preserve the sum of squared couplings: the cylinder pattern remains at reduced depth, with the same aggregate coupling energy. No fuel delivery changes. Bring out coherent pressure harmonics and 550-3600 Hz block modes; use 9 ms base decay and rounded 3 ms attack/8 ms loaded decay. Smooth valve contacts at 0.65 ms excite 1650/2755 Hz modes; the prior 1.8 ms contact strongly attenuated its own 1050 Hz resonance. Increase valve-window-gated intake breath and flow-driven exhaust detail. These are artistic radiation parameters and a listening perspective, not identified engine hardware. Source-preview total energy is dominated by bass; matching that fraction alone hid the upper layers. Version 12 retains the per-boundary native motored-force channel. No solved turbo/ECU, accessory drive, injector needle acoustics, road, cabin or free-running noise layer is claimed. Perceptual approval pending. Small clanking adjustment after the reduced-modulation audition: raise valve contact gain from .028 to .035 and ring decay from 1.8 to 2.2 ms. Keep the 0.65 ms smooth contact attack, modal frequencies, reduced cylinder contrast, intake, exhaust and combustion radiation unchanged. This emphasizes existing valve/body contact radiation; no new sample, extra impact event or harder combustion pulse is added."
    }
  }
